  "_doc": "Placeable ship components. Content is data: add an entry here and it can be placed. size is [w, h] in cells at rotation 0 (a crew body is 2x2 cells, so a 1-cell corridor is too narrow). power: positive produces, negative consumes. priority: lower is powered first when power is short (0 for producers and zero-power parts). tier: 1 to 3 (Mk1 to Mk3). family groups related parts. manned: works better with crew. stats: numbers read by the systems that use the part. line: scrap, standard or neon (data/lines.json). hp: system health, at 0 it is disabled until repaired. heat_limit: overheats at this heat. heat_per_s: heat gained per second while running. cooling: heat lost per second. stats.cooling_bonus: extra cooling every part in the same room gets (radiator). Shield stats: stats.layers (bubble layers), stats.sectors (1, 4 or 8: how many sectors the bubble is split into) and stats.recharge (seconds until a used layer is back, default 2.0; lower is faster). unique: true marks a found-or-traded item that has no recipe. effects: tags the combat code reads for a unique or special part (for weapons they live in weapons.json). A weapon part needs an entry in weapons.json under the same id. blurb: one line of flavour.",
